WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.559
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.280
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.518
Unit twenty-four: Volunteering. In this unit, you will make suggestions for helping the community.

4
00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:17.495
Volunteer.

5
00:00:18.195 --> 00:00:21.007
Volunteer means to work for free to help others.

6
00:00:21.307 --> 00:00:23.016
I volunteer at the library.

7
00:00:23.716 --> 00:00:26.206
Your turn. Say: Volunteer.

8
00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:29.965
Volunteer.

9
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:31.684
Help.

10
00:00:32.384 --> 00:00:34.883
Help means to do something useful for someone.

11
00:00:35.183 --> 00:00:37.264
We help older people carry water.

12
00:00:37.964 --> 00:00:40.593
Your turn. Say: Help.

13
00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:44.073
Help.

14
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:46.073
Community.

15
00:00:46.773 --> 00:00:49.341
Community means the people who live in one area.

16
00:00:49.641 --> 00:00:51.490
Our community is very friendly.

17
00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.575
Your turn. Say: Community.

18
00:00:57.275 --> 00:00:58.334
Community.

19
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.142
Clean up.

20
00:01:00.842 --> 00:01:03.968
Clean up means to remove rubbish and make a place tidy.

21
00:01:04.268 --> 00:01:05.768
Let's clean up the beach.

22
00:01:06.468 --> 00:01:09.608
Your turn. Say: Clean up.

23
00:01:12.308 --> 00:01:13.170
Clean up.

24
00:01:14.183 --> 00:01:14.987
Donate.

25
00:01:15.687 --> 00:01:18.418
Donate means to give money or things to help people.

26
00:01:18.718 --> 00:01:20.137
We donated clothes.

27
00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:23.211
Your turn. Say: Donate.

28
00:01:25.911 --> 00:01:26.726
Donate.

29
00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:28.613
Elderly.

30
00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:31.162
Elderly means old (a polite word).

31
00:01:31.462 --> 00:01:33.252
We visited elderly people.

32
00:01:33.952 --> 00:01:36.628
Your turn. Say: Elderly.

33
00:01:39.328 --> 00:01:40.271
Elderly.

34
00:01:41.283 --> 00:01:42.122
Charity.

35
00:01:42.822 --> 00:01:46.249
Charity means an organisation that helps people in need.

36
00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:48.143
The charity builds wells.

37
00:01:48.843 --> 00:01:51.855
Your turn. Say: Charity.

38
00:01:54.555 --> 00:01:55.359
Charity.

39
00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.119
Kind.

40
00:01:57.819 --> 00:01:59.586
Kind means caring and helpful.

41
00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.526
Volunteers are kind people.

42
00:02:02.226 --> 00:02:05.215
Your turn. Say: Kind.

43
00:02:07.915 --> 00:02:08.637
Kind.

44
00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.638
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:11.938 --> 00:02:14.704
Sreypich, how could our class help the community?

46
00:02:16.017 --> 00:02:17.784
We could clean up the park.

47
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.109
Good idea! What else?

48
00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:24.358
We could donate books to a charity.

49
00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.417
And the elderly people nearby?

50
00:02:28.717 --> 00:02:30.414
We could visit them and read to them.

51
00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.668
Grammar focus: Could plus verb (suggestions).

52
00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:37.702
We could clean the park. We could donate books.

53
00:02:38.002 --> 00:02:40.686
'Could' makes a suggestion sound friendly and polite.

54
00:02:41.683 --> 00:02:44.243
Now read and listen. Helping Hands.

55
00:02:44.543 --> 00:02:47.158
Volunteering means helping without being paid.

56
00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.332
Our class volunteered to clean up the park last month.

57
00:02:52.617 --> 00:02:54.744
We also donated books to a charity.

58
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:59.884
Then, we visited elderly people in our community and sang songs for them.

59
00:03:01.183 --> 00:03:03.554
Being kind made us feel happy and proud.

60
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.444
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:07.744 --> 00:03:10.455
We blank donate books. (suggestion)

62
00:03:10.755 --> 00:03:14.443
A, could. B, can't. C, must not.

63
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.310
The answer is A: could.

64
00:03:21.817 --> 00:03:24.257
To give money or things to help people is to blank.

65
00:03:24.557 --> 00:03:28.896
A, donate. B, clean up. C, volunteer.

66
00:03:32.883 --> 00:03:34.848
The answer is A: donate.

67
00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.209
An organisation that helps people in need is a blank.

68
00:03:39.509 --> 00:03:43.023
A, charity. B, community. C, volunteer.

69
00:03:47.017 --> 00:03:49.341
The answer is A: charity.

70
00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:54.350
Now it's your turn to speak. How could you volunteer in your community?

71
00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:04.656
I could teach young children to read, and my friends and I could clean up the pagoda on weekends.

72
00:04:04.956 --> 00:04:06.991
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:07.983 --> 00:04:12.575
Great work today! You learned eight new words and could plus verb (suggestions).

74
00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:16.874
Today's value is helping others. Give your time to help people in need.

75
00:04:17.174 --> 00:04:20.174
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

76
00:04:20.474 --> 00:04:23.510
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

